full_text:
The Council of PR Firms yesterday urged PR firms to "pledge" to Wikipedia that they will only submit materials to  the online encyclopedia that are true and accurate.
The Council of PR Firms, which represents about 400 PR agencies, has launched a campaign to promote best practices for online content creation and sharing. The campaign is called "PR Pledge," and it aims to encourage PR professionals to submit accurate and reliable information to online platforms such as Wikipedia, Twitter, and blogs.
The PR Pledge encourages PR firms to commit to the following principles:
* To only submit accurate and reliable information to online platforms;
* To clearly disclose their affiliation with a particular organization or individual when submitting content;
* To respect the rules and guidelines of each online platform;

